{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/90371-multi-cover-question","id":90371,"title":"Multi-Cover Question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-13T12:13:30-07:00","id":90371,"title":"Multi-Cover Question","content":"I've not seen a similar thread with the question I'm confused about, but maybe I'm missing an obvious answer. What happens when a demon leaves one cover for another? Does he blink transform into that cover or does he eject from the body and suddenly appear in the other? In the same sense what happens to that other cover? example: Demon has two covers, both families. One he's a dad the other she's the mom. Both families he has a wife/husband and a child. what happens when he wants to swap genders and check on the other family? Does he just become she and have to sneak out the house and drive across down switch cars and go to the other house? What happens to one family when he's in the other cover do they just think &quot;mom's on a business trip again?&quot; or do they just auto pilot with out him? I love the game so far as I'm reading it, but this doesn't make too much sense. Mostly because I'm not getting a clear picture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2191-kevorkiandoctor","name":"Kevorkiandoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T19:00:08-07:00","id":90553,"title":"","content":"From what I've gather the Demon has to become each cover for that cover to interact with the world. Sorta like wearing a costume. If our Demon has two covers than it would need to slide from one cover to become the next; just as if it were changing clothes the Demon still occupies the same space. So our Demon is Mr. X being a father at his son's little league game. He'd have to become Mrs. Y, then drive over from their to her daughter's parent teacher conference. If you've ever watched Pokemon, you know how Jame's dresses up? Alot, well when James is pretending to be a girl here, James the team rocket member isn't present there. <br /> Maintaining strong covers like that is supposed to be hard, that's sorta the fun. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T21:30:20-07:00","id":90642,"title":"","content":"Yea, your basically juggling a bunch of hot potatoes. To be fair, there have been real people who have lived lies, and have had multiple families without the other families knowing about it. Running from one family to another, usually saying they have business meetings and such, doing it for years, this is all without any supernatural abilities.<br /> <br /> It does seem like it could get messy fast though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2356-badmojo","name":"Badmojo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T06:44:01-07:00","id":91595,"title":"","content":"Yes, you have to do that, juggling lives.<br /> <br /> The transformation is in the blink of an eye, a flip of a switch. So that part is easy. Its the actual need to maintain high level covers of multiple kinds that can be a drain on your time and resources. That said...<br /> <br /> <br /> You could be a working mom in one Cover. That &quot;job&quot; doesn't actually exist - you're really going out, swapping Covers, and then acting as a gangster smuggling guns. Maybe another day, you head out to do work at a bar instead of gangster work.<br /> <br /> <br /> Here's the thing about Covers. There's holes in them that can be found if you look. Because they're not real - they're just fakes. You don't actually do half the things your Cover says they do.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-15-2014, 09:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T07:41:19-07:00","id":91620,"title":"","content":"So if I bought &quot;Plays Tennis Every Sunday with the Boss&quot; from someone in a pact, would I actually have to go play Tennis with the Boss every sunday for it to count, or would I run into the boss every monday, where he has manufactured memories of our game?<br /> <br /> I guess my question is, how much if any is the Demon's life automated?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 03-15-2014, 11:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T11:00:44-07:00","id":91738,"title":"","content":"From what I understand you have to run maintenance on your cover to keep your cover rating up or else it goes down. If your cover is expected to play tennis with the boss every sunday, then your expected to play with the boss every sunday. You can skip out every so often &quot;oh, little tim is sick and I need to take him to the doctor&quot;, &quot;Oh, car broke down&quot;..etc, but like in real life, the excuses will run thin fast, unless you buy a cover from someone who is known to make promises/appointments and never keep them, then you will be in character when you do not show up..etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> You can always trade out pact covers, sell that piece of cover to another demon (can you burn pieces of cover or is that only for a complete cover?) and upgrade to something that works out better for your character. You can also gradually change things with time. People are not static, things change. So you play with the boss every sunday, and then gradually change things where you tell the boss you will have projects coming up or some other reason so you will not be going to play tennis every so often and etc. If it is believable excuse then I would argue that would not hurt your cover rating. However, if the boss checks up on you for whatever reason and you are not doing what you said you were doing, then your character would take a hit.<br /> <br /> Basically, it is a spy game, you need to do enough that everyone believes you are the person you pretend to be without raising red flags that you are living a double life. People are suspicious and gossipy by nature, so you have to be careful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2356-badmojo","name":"Badmojo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T13:34:14-07:00","id":91822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/90371-multi-cover-question?p=91620#post91620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if I bought &quot;Plays Tennis Every Sunday with the Boss&quot; from someone in a pact, would I actually have to go play Tennis with the Boss every sunday for it to count, or would I run into the boss every monday, where he has manufactured memories of our game?<br /> <br /> I guess my question is, how much if any is the Demon's life automated?</div> </div> </div> </div> You have to actually act it out, or that part of your Cover degrades. Avoiding it counts as &quot;acting out of Cover.&quot; <br /> <br /> The whole &quot;reality accommodates you&quot; bit only happens when 1) you're an angel with an active Infrastructure to back you, 2) the moment of your Fall, and 3) at the moment a pact is sealed. Everything else has to either be done the normal way, actually living it out.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T14:58:07-07:00","id":91863,"title":"","content":"Does the other person actually exist too? So I get &quot;tennis with boss on weekend&quot; dies the other guy actually exist somewhere else during that time as well? Or does he blink out while I play my tennis game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2191-kevorkiandoctor","name":"Kevorkiandoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T15:54:17-07:00","id":91903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kevorkiandoctor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/90371-multi-cover-question?p=91863#post91863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the other person actually exist too? So I get &quot;tennis with boss on weekend&quot; dies the other guy actually exist somewhere else during that time as well? Or does he blink out while I play my tennis game?</div> </div> </div> </div>Covers do not fabricate people wholesale, and pacts alter the memories of direct parties to the exchange of connections to suit. The boss exists, because a) the aforementioned lack of wholesale spontaneous generation of individuals and b) odds are good you got &quot;tennis with boss on weekend&quot; from somebody who actually played tennis with their boss on the weekends before they traded that aspect of their life to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T16:14:56-07:00","id":91912,"title":"","content":"Yea, your basically taking pieces of other peoples lives and adding it to your own. It just uses what is already there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2356-badmojo","name":"Badmojo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T19:15:09-07:00","id":92031,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry maybe I'm not tracking. So in a sense if I shift into the guy who play tennis with boss, where is that guy? The real guy? Off at his apartment? Or does he stop existing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2191-kevorkiandoctor","name":"Kevorkiandoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T19:27:09-07:00","id":92041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kevorkiandoctor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/90371-multi-cover-question?p=92031#post92031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry maybe I'm not tracking. So in a sense if I shift into the guy who play tennis with boss, where is that guy? The real guy? Off at his apartment? Or does he stop existing?</div> </div> </div> </div>The connective details of your other Covers' lives do not vanish when you assume a different form. Your brown-noser still has his weekly tennis appointment with the boss, and if he misses it because he's busy being the mousy librarian across town, he'll have to explain himself when he next encounters his boss.<br /> <br /> If he goes for long enough without showing up to work (or anywhere else), the brown-noser Cover will just sort of gradually disintegrate and presumably everybody will forget about him, while the librarian, who has kept all their appointments and made the necessary appearances, will still be around, barring some aberrant situation.<br /> <br /> The primary exception is that Cover-Linked Boltholes disappear completely when you're not in the Cover they're linked to, but seeing as a Bolthole is a single windowless room where a single windowless room should not be, that's not exactly a huge concern.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T13:03:05-07:00","id":92937,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... if you purchase this tennis with the boss method... do you end up playing tennis with the original owner's boss (who isn't your boss unless you also purchase the guy's job), or your own boss for that cover? If the former, it could lead to confusion.. does the boss think you work for him? Or does he not know why he plays tennis with a stranger and makes up his own excuses? Does he not notice or care, just showing up to play and have casual chat with you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T14:22:41-07:00","id":92976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/90371-multi-cover-question?p=92937#post92937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm... if you purchase this tennis with the boss method... do you end up playing tennis with the original owner's boss (who isn't your boss unless you also purchase the guy's job), or your own boss for that cover? If the former, it could lead to confusion.. does the boss think you work for him? Or does he not know why he plays tennis with a stranger and makes up his own excuses? Does he not notice or care, just showing up to play and have casual chat with you?</div> </div> </div> </div>my understanding of it is this:<br /> <br /> you gain &quot;tennis with the boss&quot; from a pact.<br /> <br /> I believe you gain tennis with the pacted individual's boss. The fine details of what that all entails is something you should work out with your ST and remember; t's okay if the details do not work out perfectly. Covers can have some inconsistencies.<br /> The main thing to remember are the people/objects involved and the relationship between the pacted individual and those things. I would suggest that if the boss looked favourably upon the pacted individual that the boss continue to look favourably on the demon even though the details regarding why they are now playing tennis with someone completely different can confuse outside observers.<br /> <br /> My suggestion is, the higher your cover, the harder it is to find inconsistencies. So if you had a cover maybe 9 or 10, this bit of cover may integrate seamlessly into your current cover with no conflicts whatsoever. <br /> Lower cover scores might have more glaring issues. like the boss himself questioning why they are playing tennis with you, but they continue to play tennis with you anyway.<br /> <br /> as for your other questions:<br /> It's possible that the boss can think you work for them, but it's also possible that you may now work for this individual in some minor way. After all &quot;boss&quot; is a very important part of the relationship you pacted for. It doesn't have to be the pacted individual's job, per se. (after all that wasn't part of the deal). But it is important that this person is your &quot;boss&quot;.<br /> You could be a stranger to this person (possibly a new hire).<br /> The boss could notice and could care that all depends.<br /> <br /> The fine details are up for you and your ST to work out (feel free to help them out by suggesting some reasonable explanations). <br /> Also remember that covers made out of patchwork details like this are more fragile than other covers until they reach a certain rating.<br /> <br /> <br /> As to where your covers &quot;go&quot; when not in use.<br /> All of these covers stay with you. They age in real time.<br /> When you shift out of tennis with boss guy. He doesn't leave you or suddenly appear in his apartment doing things independently of you. <br /> He also does not &quot;stop existing&quot;. his life, such as it is, continues without his presence and if he continually fails to fulfil his obligations, you may compromise that cover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1930-rixx","name":"Rixx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T04:31:39-07:00","id":93383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kevorkiandoctor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/90371-multi-cover-question?p=92031#post92031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry maybe I'm not tracking. So in a sense if I shift into the guy who play tennis with boss, where is that guy? The real guy? Off at his apartment? Or does he stop existing?</div> </div> </div> </div>If I'm reading you correctly, you're asking what happens to the person who signed the pact with you. The answer is: as long as it isn't a soul pact, they keep on existing, they just...lose the bits that they traded away. Someone who traded away their relationship with their boss has essentially been replaced by the demon when it comes to that relationship and probably in regards with that job as whole - the demon is the one who plays tennis with the boss, who catered the Christmas party last year, who's been skipped over for promotions a few times due to office politics but the boss feels kinda guilty so they share a whiskey after long days. The guy who signed that all away remembers all that - he's the only one who's directly connected who does, actually - but the point of the pact is that it's not part of his life anymore, so he just doesn't go into work anymore. He might have to get a new job if he didn't sign up for enough riches to live without working, and if he ever meets someone who was only tangentially related that remembers that -he- used to work at their company, well, that could get a little awkward.<br /> <br /> To sum it up, as long as it isn't a soulpact that's called in the person who's involved in a pact is perfectly fine physically - they still exist. The more they've traded away, the more drastic their life changes however as the demon replaces him in all that context, leaving holes in his life that he has to fill back up, emotionally speaking. Imagine what you'd have to do if you sold someone your job, your smoking habit, your girlfriend, or the fact that you have - had - siblings. It can be very weird knowing that someone's living part of your life, and that the part of your life in question isn't actually yours anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T06:49:38-07:00","id":93448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/90371-multi-cover-question?p=92937#post92937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm... if you purchase this tennis with the boss method... do you end up playing tennis with the original owner's boss (who isn't your boss unless you also purchase the guy's job), or your own boss for that cover? If the former, it could lead to confusion.. does the boss think you work for him? Or does he not know why he plays tennis with a stranger and makes up his own excuses? Does he not notice or care, just showing up to play and have casual chat with you?</div> </div> </div> </div> You purchase tennis with &quot;Frank Joe Smith&quot; who happens to be the pactee's boss. <br /> <br /> All of Frank's memories of playing tennis are now replaced with memories of playing with the demon, so he doesn't notice anything strange. The boss's friends may, but Frank himself won't. They discuss work sometimes, but the demon might not work there. Its just a comfortable topic for some reason. <br /> <br /> The pactee, meanwhile, loses any favoritism he might have gained from playing tennis with the boss.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, chances are the pactee actually ended up trading away his entire relationship with his boss - including his job. But if they were friends outside of work, they might have just traded that friendship. Its relationships the demon is after, not specific habits or stuff. The demon wants to take friends, family, jobs, histories to shore up his Cover. Playing tennis alone is probably not going to help much to justify the risk of making a pact in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}